{{--
  Terms of service (plan §22.7) — code-defined, owned by the Landing module.

  TEMPLATE COPY. A starting structure, not legal advice, and it names no
  company. Replace the bracketed parts, have it reviewed, and remove the
  notice at the top before launch.
--}}
@component('layouts/marketing', {
  title: 'Terms of service',
  description: `The terms that apply when you use ${appName}.`,
})
  <article class="content-article">
    <div class="info-box info-box-warning" style="margin-bottom: 32px">
      Template text. Replace the bracketed details and have this reviewed before launch.
    </div>

    <header class="content-article-header">
      <h1 class="content-article-title">Terms of service</h1>
      <div class="content-article-meta">Last updated [date]</div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        These terms are an agreement between you and [company name] ("we") about your use of
        {{ appName }}. By creating an account you accept them. If you use {{ appName }} for an
        organisation, you accept them on its behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        Keep your sign-in details secure and tell us at [support email] if you think someone else
        has used them. You are responsible for what happens under your account and in your
        workspace.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        What you put into {{ appName }} remains yours. You give us permission to store and process
        it only to run the service for you.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not use {{ appName }} to break the law, to infringe others' rights, to send spam, or to
        interfere with the service or other customers.
      </p>

      <h2>Plans and payment</h2>
      <p>
        Paid plans are billed in advance through [payment provider], our merchant of record. If a
        payment fails or a plan lapses, your workspace keeps its data but may stop allowing new
        items until it is back within its plan.
      </p>

      <h2>Ending the agreement</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using {{ appName }} and delete your workspace at any time. We may suspend or
        close an account that breaks these terms. [Describe notice and data-export arrangements.]
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>[Warranty disclaimer and limitation of liability — have these drafted for your jurisdiction.]</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change these terms in a way that matters, we will tell you in the app before they take effect.</p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>[Jurisdiction.]</p>
    </div>
  </article>
@end
